<%# "Forgot your password?" — POSTs `user[email]` to Devise's password path, which
    mails the reset instructions. Devise is configured paranoid, so the response never
    reveals whether the address exists; the error summary below is therefore reachable
    only for a malformed submit.

    HOOJAH 2026 (Phase 1.1) — the same restyle as log-in/sign-up: no white card
    panel, `bg-surface` page, one 52px `bg-card-2` field row. No "or / Continue
    with Google" divider and no password reveal toggle here — there is no
    password field on this screen, and this is a single-purpose recovery flow
    rather than a second entry point into the app.
%>
<div class="min-h-screen bg-surface flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-12">
  <div class="w-full max-w-sm">
    <%= render "devise/shared/brand" %>

    <h1 class="mt-6 text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-ink">Forgot your password?</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Enter your email and we'll send you reset instructions.</p>

    <%= form_for(resource, as: resource_name, url: password_path(resource_name), html: {method: :post}) do |f| %>
      <%= render "devise/shared/error_messages", resource: resource %>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 h-[52px] px-4 rounded-xl bg-card-2 border border-field">
          <%= lucide_icon "mail", class: "w-[19px] h-[19px] text-faint shrink-0" %>
          <%= f.email_field :email, autofocus: true, autocomplete: "email", placeholder: "Email address",
                class: "flex-1 min-w-0 bg-transparent border-0 outline-none text-[14.5px] text-ink placeholder:text-faint" %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%= f.submit "Send me password reset instructions", class: "mt-4 w-full h-[52px] rounded-xl bg-primary text-white font-bold shadow cursor-pointer" %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "devise/shared/links" %>
  </div>
</div>
